X:612301
T:WALTZ IN PURPLE AND CLARET
R:Waltz
C:David MacAdam
N:N: Dave's notes on this tune in the ABC file.
M:3/4
L:1/4
K:D
A/G/|F>A d|f>d A|G e c|A2 A|G>e c|
[1 A>B G|F d B|A2:|2 A B c|e d c|d2||
e|:f>b a|e>g f|d c B|A2 A|e>g f|
e b a|1 ^g f g|a2 g:|2 g e c|d3|]
%
%The evening after giving a mid-winter fiddle concert at the Truro 
%Library, Dinah Mellin told me of the ethereal experience of playing 
%a waltz in a room filled with light "purple and claret" from the low, 
%late afternoon mid-winter sun. This unusual color combination evoked 
%in me this waltz, my opus 1. For me its writing was a sudden awakening 
%of almost religious intensity. I could actually write tunes. [2007.02.07] 
%(rev. 2020.11.13)

